@startuml
title P2 Streamed Track - Ingest, Buffered Start and Seek

autonumber
actor User
participant "Pulsar App" as App
participant "Coordinator" as Coord
participant "Variant Pipeline" as Variant
database "Media Store" as Store
participant "Node A" as NodeA
participant "Node B" as NodeB
participant "Range API" as Range

User -> App : Select long audio\nchoose queue or replace
App -> Coord : SubmitMedia(audio_track)
Coord -> Variant : validate + transcode\ncanonical compressed variants
Variant -> Store : media ready + variant rows
Variant --> Coord : media_id + metadata

App -> Coord : CreateTransmission(queue|replace)
Coord -> Coord : Freeze target snapshot\nand queue position
Coord -> NodeA : stream_load(media_id, variant, start=0)
Coord -> NodeB : stream_load(media_id, variant, start=0)

NodeA -> Range : GET variant bytes\nRange: bytes=0-...
NodeB -> Range : GET variant bytes\nRange: bytes=0-...
Range --> NodeA : 206 Partial Content
Range --> NodeB : 206 Partial Content
NodeA -> NodeA : fill disk cache + decoder ring\nuntil buffer threshold
NodeB -> NodeB : fill disk cache + decoder ring\nuntil buffer threshold
NodeA --> Coord : stream_ready(buffered_ms)
NodeB --> Coord : stream_ready(buffered_ms)
Coord -> NodeA : resume_at(T)
Coord -> NodeB : resume_at(T)
NodeA --> Coord : started
NodeB --> Coord : started

== Seek while playing ==

User -> App : Seek to position P
App -> Coord : seek current track to P
Coord -> NodeA : stream_seek(P)
Coord -> NodeB : stream_seek(P)
NodeA -> Range : GET variant bytes\nRange: mapped to P
NodeB -> Range : GET variant bytes\nRange: mapped to P
Range --> NodeA : 206 Partial Content
Range --> NodeB : 206 Partial Content
NodeA -> NodeA : rebuild decoder ring\nat position P
NodeB -> NodeB : rebuild decoder ring\nat position P
NodeA --> Coord : stream_ready(P)
NodeB --> Coord : stream_ready(P)
Coord -> NodeA : resume_at(T2)
Coord -> NodeB : resume_at(T2)

note over Coord,Range
Delete, report or actor disable must revoke
future range fetches without changing media_id.
Cache eviction is tolerated by re-fetching the
required ranges instead of full download.
end note

@enduml
